===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[sealed]], [[airtight]] [[chamber]], such as in a manned [[spacecraft]] or [[submarine]], used to provide [[access]] to and from the [[sealed]] area without allowing air out or water in.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 March 23|author=Paul Bigland|title=HS2 is just 'passing through'|journal=RAIL|issue=953|page=42|text=At the head of the machine, we are shown the '''airlock''' through which people have to pass to work on the cutting head, as it operates under pressure to prevent leakages into the tunnel.}}
# {{lb|en|architecture|informal}} A {{l|en|vestibule}}, {{l|en|foyer}} or {{l|en|entranceway}} with doors to the exterior on one end and doors to the interior on the other, functioning to keep indoor and outdoor air, humidity, and air temperatures separate.
#: {{cot|en|mudroom|boot room}}
